%description:

TcpCubic.c:invalid -- a constant of 0 stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code accepts a constant above 0.

The classes: rfc9438 (0.4, the default, the value of RFC 9438), other (another value above 0),
invalid (0 and less). The code: at the start of an epoch, K = cbrt((W_max - cwnd) / C)
(TcpCubic::update()).

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.c
%# class: invalid
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.c
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicCInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.c = 0    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
c must be more than 0, but it is 0
